# ️ Database

The current database is:

```text
build_and_bloom
```

Main tables include:

```text
users
locations
crops
crop_requirements
planting_calendar
recommendations
weather_records
planting_plans
```

### Important Relationships

```text
users
  │
  ├── recommendations
  │
  └── planting_plans
          │
          ├── crops
          └── locations


crops
  │
  ├── crop_requirements
  ├── planting_calendar
  ├── recommendations
  └── planting_plans


locations
  │
  ├── users
  ├── planting_calendar
  ├── recommendations
  ├── weather_records
  └── planting_plans
```

---

#  Authentication

The current development version uses client-side authentication persistence through:

```text
localStorage
```

The stored user information is associated with:

```text
buildAndBloomUser
```

Protected pages currently include:

```text
/dashboard
/crops
/crops/[id]
/assessment
/weather
/calendar
/plants
/plants/plan
```

Public pages include:

```text
/
/login
/register
```

> ️ This is currently a development-stage authentication implementation. Production-grade authentication/session security can be implemented later.

---

# ️ Weather API

The backend uses OpenWeatherMap for weather information.

The API key is stored in the backend `.env` file.

Example:

```env
OPENWEATHER_API_KEY=YOUR_API_KEY
```

### Important

**Do not commit `.env` to GitHub.**

Make sure `.gitignore` contains:

```text
.env
.env.local
node_modules/
.next/
```

